  "answer": "To reduce the risk of stakeholders becoming skeptical and slow to adopt AI systems because they do not understand why specific decisions were made, it has been proposed to deploy counterfactual explanation modules in AI decision systems for end-user transparency (https://arxiv.org/abs/2001.07417). This is implemented through a heuristic search mechanism for minimal-cost counterfactual feature sets, where an algorithm removes features that most reduce the decision score per unit cost, thereby efficiently finding small or cheap explanations that directly link evidence to the outcome (https://arxiv.org/abs/2001.07417)."
